                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "Xnkb4",
                              "name": "source",
                              "fill": "$text-1",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "---\nname: daily-brief\ndescription: Produce Jason's daily trading brief — the fixed 8-section format (book, management, risk, news, hot tape, earnings map, day-trade candidates, action table), delivered in chat AND stored verbatim at the head of the day's trading log. Use when delivering any trading session brief, or when Jason asks for \"today's brief\".\n---\n\n# Daily Brief\n\nThe output contract for every trading session brief. The `trading-daily` skill runs the session; this skill defines what Jason receives. **Rules live in `trading/system.md` — this skill formats, it never defines or amends rules.**\n\n## When\n\n- **Pre-open run (~09:00 ET):** the FULL 8-section brief.\n- **Post-open run (~10:00 ET):** a DELTA brief — fills verified, stop status, what changed since pre-open — plus the action table. Never duplicate the full template an hour later.\n\n## The eight sections, fixed order (adopted 2026-08-13, Jason-directed)\n\n1. **Book** — positions table, broker-verified: qty, entry, last/pre price, P&L, stop, distance to stop. Never narrative numbers.\n2. **Management** — per-position instruction for today: trail / trim / exit / hold, fail lines due, named deadlines.\n3. **Risk** — the three books (initial-capital / giveback / gap-stress, system.md §4) as $ and % of equity, plus the capacity line for any armed spec.|",
                              "lineHeight": 1.6,
                              "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                              "fontSize": 12,
                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
